/-!
# Nonbinary linear-three MS source reductions

The original LinearThreeMSPair supplies relative normality, its literal
product, the proper odd-index radical witness, the actual FF action,
and positive even MS93 geometry with the edge-centralizer condition.
Both the original graph and the characteristic replacement retain msQ.
The SL₃ scalar center is retained, including at field four.

The whole initial moved space splits from its component-fixed complement
and is natural or doubled natural of the original field degree. The
central-omega centralizer is exactly the two-core, and the full component
marking agrees with the original quotient projection. The actual initial
commutator now has a natural or doubled-natural section model over the
original field, splits from its fixed complement, and lies in Z(msQ).

The centralizer of the whole msQ is contained in the original two-core.
If msQ is abelian, MS3 forces it to be elementary abelian and supplies an
FF-offender on its entire faithful centralizer-quotient action. These
statements apply to the original core. When it centralizes O₂(KR), it is
exactly the initial moved group and has whole natural or doubled-natural
sections; abelianity of O₂(KR) suffices. An actual natural whole-core section
also proves every short-group clause and the actual SL₃ block model.
For each of the three nonblock section rows, odd-index averaging now splits
the actual Sylow omega into its section-fixed and component-fixed factors
and computes its centralizer in the original join. This does not use
ambient centrality of the fourth row's fixed factor. The general
noncentral-core sections remain open.

For abelian Q away from field four, its intrinsic component action now
descends faithfully to the original full SL₃ quotient. This uses the actual
perfect central cover and retains conjugation on the whole core. Its binary
representation is fully generated by component commutators. An offender on
this descended action and its natural/doubled recognition remain open, as
does elimination of the exceptional field-four covering kernel.

For nonabelian Q too, the entire Z(Q), Ω₁(Z(Q)), and [Z(Q),K] now
admit faithful actions of the original full SL₃ outside field four. The
whole center consequently centralizes intrinsic O₂(K). At every nonbinary
field, MS3 supplies an FF action on the entire Ω₁(Z(Q)) through its literal
centralizer quotient. Their natural-section recognition, exceptional
covering kernels and the Frattini sections remain open.

On the entire central omega, and on an abelian whole core, the same original
maximum elementary subgroup now gives best offenders on the whole and initial
actions. Its whole-action image escapes the two-core, and the full covering
component lies in the whole-section best-offender group, including at field
four. The comparison to the initial action has exactly the whole actor's
two-core as kernel. Eliminating that remaining action kernel and recognizing
the whole sections are still required.

The entire Q/Φ(Q) now has its literal action kernel inside O₂(KR) and a
marked perfect central SL₃ cover. Outside field four its full faithful
SL₃ representation is generated by component displacements, and
[O₂(K),Q] lies in Φ(Q), also for nonabelian Q. Its module recognition
and the exceptional covering kernel remain open.

The separate field-four original F4 candidate now has its literal MS3
condition proved, using exceptional duality over the original coefficient
field. The same candidate is normal in its original parabolic, perfect,
and exactly its solvable residual and two-residual. Its full SL₃ quotient,
C-component, two-core, fitting, SQTK and Sylow/radical clauses remain
uncertified; no full nonbinary counterexample is asserted.

Outside field four the original msQ now equals the full intrinsic O₂(K),
including for nonabelian Q. The proof uses the perfect central cover
K/[O₂(K),K] and the ordinary multiplier theorem. Thus a strict difference
between these two cores is confined to field four. The noncentral source whole-section
models and their remaining radical inequalities remain open.

The actual Sylow omega now splits unconditionally over the S-fixed initial
moved factor and Ω₁(Z(KR)), with no whole-core model or abelianity premise.
It is noncentral at every nonbinary field, including field four. Its literal
centralizer and two-core comparison pass exactly to the faithful initial
module action. In the doubled initial branch, common-axis best offenders
cannot lie in the point radical, proving the original radical inequality
for every supplied Sylow overgroup. Thus the initial moved group has natural
order or all those strict inequalities hold. The whole central-core branch
now satisfies complete C.1.34 alternatives, including at field four; an
abelian O₂(KR) suffices. The general noncentral-core analysis remains open.

For an actual doubled whole-core model, the original radical comparison
now passes exactly to that whole action at every field. In every nonbinary field degree,
the full normalizer offender estimate proves its radical inequality without
centrality in O₂(KR), including at field four. The supplied whole-core marking is retained in the
completed second alternative and the original Chapter4/Chapter11 applications.

If the whole center or its whole moved subgroup is natural, it now equals
the initial moved subgroup. In the moved-center branch the entire center
centralizes O₂(K), has a faithful action of the original full SL₃ even at
field four, and splits over its K-fixed subgroup. Recognition of that
whole natural moved center and identification of the fixed factor with
C_Q(K) remain open; no ambient centrality of that factor is inferred.

The whole upper Frattini sections now identify C_Q(K) with the K-fixed
subgroup of the entire center. Thus the natural moved-center branch splits
Z(Q) over the actual whole fixed factor. In the natural-center/doubled-dual
row that fixed factor is trivial. An independently trivial C_Q(K) also
promotes a natural moved center to the whole natural center. The original
nonblock line-parabolic configuration supplies that triviality.

When C_Q(K)=1, every nontrivial subgroup of Q normalized by K and the join
two-core meets the initial moved layer. Nonidentity quotient scalars therefore
act fixed-freely on the whole center, including at field four. Actual cubic
lifts show that the whole center equals its component commutator. The original
nonblock configuration discharges the fixed-factor premise; no whole-section
model or trivial even covering kernel is used in this argument.

The whole-core analysis and remaining radical inequalities remain required
for MSModuleAlternatives in C.1.34. The nonblock consumer applies the proved
results to its original configuration without Hypothesis1223.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith C.1.31--34, pp.135--137; MS93, pp.828--831,
854--857,863,932--933.
-/
